Z||000000||FieroDancer||06-19-2001||03:32 PM||||Living in New York City and having a Fiero is a daunting task apparently. Anyone know of a good mechanic around here or maybe even in Connecticut? I tried a dealer in NJ (the only dealer who actually work on Fiero's around here) and while the work was actually good (and the cost outright ridiculous), I'd like to find a Fiero knowledgeable mechanic - even if I have to drive a ways away. My engine seem to have a fuel delivery problem - even started backfiring some.<BR>Any help would be appreciated. I love my 87 Fiero - my second one.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||06-19-2001||07:22 PM||||87 4 or 6 cyl? tell us more about it. I've put a very large amount of info that is 87-88 4 cylinder specific in my cave.<P>Just what is making you think the problem is fuel delivery? ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroDancer||06-19-2001||08:27 PM||||Thank you for your reply. It is a 4 cyl Fiero. I have to figure out how to access your cave. I'm new to this (and any) online forum. <BR>The engine never dies on me and idles just fine, but stutters when I drive, then goes away for a little while, then back to as if the fuel delivery is being hampered - light for service engine soon goes on at the same time, then goes away. Any ideas?  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||fyerstarter||06-19-2001||09:57 PM||||I don't think the check engine light will come on for a fuel problem. I could be wrong. Anyway pull the little cover off where the cigarrette lighter is and ground the top and bottom terminals closest to the passenger side with a paper clip or wire. Watch the check engine light and it should flash you a code. Like this.<P>1 flash....pause....2 flashes  = 12<P>It should flash a 12, then your codes, and then a 12 again when it's done. <P>Once you get the code look it up in the archives or post it here and people may be able to help you with your problem   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by fyerstarter (edited 06-19-2001).]||||reg||1
